<div class="page">
  <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">6. PROGRAMME MATERIALS</h3>
  <p>Online Materials will be based on the applicable norms laid down by competent authority of UGC and provided to the students as and when necessary. These e-learning Materials in Four-Quadrant approach using various collaboration enablers made available in SWAYAM/LMS and these digital contents will also be made accessible to all the registered candidates in a streamlined way with proper access credentials.</p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">7. TEACHING & LEARNING METHODOLOGY</h3>
  <p>The teaching and learning methodology will be as per the UGC-OL Regulations 2018.</p>

  <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">8. EVALUATION SYSTEM FOR VARIOUS PROGRAMMES</h3>
  <p>The courses will be offered in semester pattern. For each course that the student is undergoing during a semester, there is a Continuous Internal Assessment (CIA) mark, for a maximum of 30 marks, based on the student's performance in the proctored online - assessments, seminar, quiz, assignment, etc. There will be one proctored online examination of 3 hours duration at the end of the semester for each credited course.</p>
  <p>Out of a total of 100 marks allotted for each course 30 marks are allotted for continuous internal assessment and 70 marks for the end semester examination</p>

  <h4 style="margin-top: 20px;">8.4. Course-wise grades are awarded to the students by adopting the following scheme, based on the aggregate marks scored by the student in the course (which includes internal assessment marks and end-semester examination marks)</h4>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 15%;">RANGE</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">LETTER GRADE</th>
        <th style="width: 15%;">GRADE POINT</th>
        <th style="width: 55%;">DESCRIPTION OF PERFORMANCE</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>&ge;91%</td>
        <td>S</td>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>Outstanding</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>&ge;80% and &lt; 90%</td>
        <td>A+</td>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>Excellent</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>&ge;70% and &lt; 80%</td>
        <td>A</td>
        <td>8</td>
        <td>Very Good</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>&ge;60% and &lt; 70%</td>
        <td>B</td>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>Good</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>&ge;50% and &lt; 60%</td>
